+| Booking a visit can rewrite the owner it is booked under *(derived, unconfirmed, found 2026-08-06)* | `REQ-VIS-001` | `VisitController.processNewVisitForm` binds request parameters onto the `Owner` loaded for the request and then saves that owner. The binder disallows `id` and `*.id` only, so a booking POST carrying owner fields — or `pets[n]` fields, since `Owner.getPets` hands out the live list — persists them alongside the visit. Correcting contact details is `REQ-OWN-004`'s flow, not booking's. The cancel handler on the same controller takes its owner with binding switched off and is unaffected |
